Pre-requisite
=============

Install the SDL library with the following command:

sudo apt-get install libsdl1.2-dev

Build
=====

Launch ./fetch.sh to fetch QEMU 8.0.0 and to apply the path for framebuffer and input support.

QEMU Configuration and compilation
==================================

Configure options:

AArch32 version:

./configure --target-list=arm-softmmu --disable-attr --disable-werror --disable-docs

AArch64 version:

./configure --target-list=aarch64-softmmu --disable-attr --disable-werror --disable-docs

Both versions:

./configure --target-list=arm-softmmu,aarch64-softmmu --disable-attr --disable-werror --disable-docs

To build:

make -j<#cpus>


If you have a black screen when running QEMU, try to use gtk backend instead.
To do this, first make sure you have the gtk3 libraries:

sudo apt-get install libavahi-ui-gtk3-dev

and use the following configuration (for Aarch64 as example)

./configure --target-list=arm-softmmu,aarch64-softmmu --enable-gtk --disable-attr --disable-werror --disable-docs

This should solve the issue of black screen.

